# This repo is checked out on both Windows (core.autocrlf=true) and accessed
# from WSL/Linux (via the same checkout, over /mnt/c) as one shared working
# copy. Without this file, Windows' autocrlf silently checks the bash/*
# configs out with CRLF, which bash then fails to source at all (a stray \r
# breaks `foo() {` one-liners and corrupts `source ~/.bash_git` into a path
# that doesn't exist) - it looks like "nothing got set up" even though the
# symlinks themselves are fine. Force LF on anything a POSIX shell reads,
# regardless of platform; leave PowerShell/JSON/Lua alone since both line
# endings work fine there.
bash/**    text eol=lf
install.sh text eol=lf
*.sh       text eol=lf
ripgrep/** text eol=lf
